00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:10,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:11,458 --> 00:00:13,208
Our camp is just up ahead.

2
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:15,566
Turn right at that intersection
and we're there.

3
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:20,117
Slow down.

4
00:00:32,175 --> 00:00:33,950
It's just ahead.

5
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,158
This is my home.

6
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,342
Mom!

7
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:52,467
Cheng Ren!

8
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:53,467
Your leg...

9
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,842
How... How did this happen?

10
00:00:55,842 --> 00:00:57,208
It hurts so much.

11
00:00:57,208 --> 00:01:00,283
Quick, get inside! Hurry!

12
00:02:04,304 --> 00:02:09,066
[Apocalypse Log 7]

13
00:02:18,467 --> 00:02:20,425
After your father died,

14
00:02:20,425 --> 00:02:22,867
it's just been the two of us.

15
00:02:25,383 --> 00:02:28,408
If something happens to you,

16
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,825
what will I do?

17
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:37,800
We have no food and no medicine.

18
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,467
This wretched place...

19
00:02:39,467 --> 00:02:42,908
We can't survive here much longer.

20
00:02:43,675 --> 00:02:44,675
And now you're...

21
00:02:44,675 --> 00:02:45,717
Mom.

22
00:02:45,717 --> 00:02:47,467
Don't cry.

23
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:48,883
It's all my fault.

24
00:02:48,883 --> 00:02:49,986
It's my fault for being useless.

25
00:02:49,986 --> 00:02:51,592
I couldn't catch any game,

26
00:02:51,592 --> 00:02:53,217
and I even got myself injured.

27
00:02:53,217 --> 00:02:54,908
I'm a burden to you.

28
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,800
Madam.

29
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,450
Please don't cry.

30
00:03:02,383 --> 00:03:03,883
We injured him by mistake.

31
00:03:03,883 --> 00:03:05,783
We will take full responsibility.

32
00:03:09,758 --> 00:03:11,658
We'll be staying here for a while.

33
00:03:18,092 --> 00:03:21,508
You've seen how things are here.

34
00:03:21,508 --> 00:03:24,383
If you don't help us,

35
00:03:24,383 --> 00:03:26,550
a widow and her son

36
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:29,533
really won't be able to survive.

37
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,467
Don't worry.

38
00:03:32,467 --> 00:03:34,783
We'll go out for food tomorrow.

39
00:03:40,883 --> 00:03:42,800
It's too late today.

40
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,092
There are some biscuits in the bag.

41
00:03:44,092 --> 00:03:45,950
Have some to tide you over.

42
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:55,441
How long have you lived here?

43
00:03:57,258 --> 00:03:59,117
Are there any zombies nearby?

44
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:03,717
It's been a while.

45
00:04:03,717 --> 00:04:07,800
Since we arrived, we haven't seen any zombies.

46
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,992
It's very safe here.

47
00:04:14,967 --> 00:04:16,783
Come with me.

48
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,783
Our space is limited.

49
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:34,883
One person can sleep here.

50
00:04:34,883 --> 00:04:36,800
But it needs to be tidied up.

51
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,342
There's a shed outside.

52
00:04:38,342 --> 00:04:40,283
One more person can sleep there.

53
00:04:42,467 --> 00:04:43,925
This place will do.

54
00:04:43,925 --> 00:04:45,008
He can...

55
00:04:45,008 --> 00:04:46,742
He'll sleep with me.

56
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:55,050
It's okay, madam.

57
00:04:55,050 --> 00:04:56,051
I'll sleep here.

58
00:04:56,051 --> 00:04:58,408
You should rest early. Don't worry about us.

59
00:05:14,675 --> 00:05:16,092
It shouldn't take too long.

60
00:05:16,092 --> 00:05:18,575
I think we can leave in a few days.

61
00:05:19,758 --> 00:05:21,325
There's no hurry.

62
00:05:22,258 --> 00:05:24,158
You're actually not in a hurry to leave?

63
00:05:25,425 --> 00:05:27,133
You saw the boat, right?

64
00:05:27,133 --> 00:05:28,675
I'll check the boat's condition tomorrow.

65
00:05:28,675 --> 00:05:31,075
We'll take the waterway once it's fixed.

66
00:05:47,883 --> 00:05:49,675
You're not sleeping yet?

67
00:05:49,675 --> 00:05:51,117
You go to sleep first.

68
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:50,717
What are you two doing?

69
00:06:50,717 --> 00:06:51,717
Don't worry, madam.

70
00:06:51,717 --> 00:06:53,908
We'll come back with food.

71
00:07:38,967 --> 00:07:40,867
The hull is mostly intact.

72
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:51,367
The fuel tank is empty.

73
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:02,783
The wires are also broken.

74
00:08:03,758 --> 00:08:06,758
If we can find wires and diesel,

75
00:08:06,758 --> 00:08:08,675
we should be able to fix it.

76
00:08:08,675 --> 00:08:10,283
Then let's go look for them.

77
00:08:24,217 --> 00:08:25,742
You still want to eat that?

78
00:08:28,258 --> 00:08:29,259
I'm not stupid.

79
00:08:29,259 --> 00:08:31,200
Last time was truly an accident.

80
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:33,342
If you don't go looking for trouble,

81
00:08:33,342 --> 00:08:35,033
there won't be any accidents.

82
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,950
<i>Mount Zhiliao.</i>

83
00:09:43,592 --> 00:09:46,770
<i>This waterway leads back to our old camp.</i>

84
00:09:46,770 --> 00:09:49,133
How's it going on your end?

85
00:09:49,133 --> 00:09:51,825
I found some usable wires.

86
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:54,742
That's everything. Let's go.

87
00:10:48,425 --> 00:10:49,508
You're back.

88
00:10:49,508 --> 00:10:51,217
You must be tired after a long day.

89
00:10:51,217 --> 00:10:52,800
I just made some soup.

90
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,675
I picked some wild vegetable leaves outside.

91
00:10:54,675 --> 00:10:56,867
Have a sip to quench your thirst.

92
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:00,950
I'm not thirsty.

93
00:11:03,133 --> 00:11:04,825
Neither of us is thirsty.

94
00:11:05,717 --> 00:11:08,283
Madam, you and your son have it.

95
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:10,717
My mom spent a long time cooking this.

96
00:11:10,717 --> 00:11:14,450
If you won't have it, then I will.

97
00:11:20,842 --> 00:11:23,117
We brought back quite a lot of things.

98
00:11:29,592 --> 00:11:31,133
You guys are amazing.

99
00:11:31,133 --> 00:11:33,258
So much good food.

100
00:11:33,258 --> 00:11:34,908
Let's split it half and half.

101
00:11:40,508 --> 00:11:46,050
I don't know when
my son's leg will fully recover.

102
00:11:46,050 --> 00:11:49,842
He can't work, and he's just a burden.

103
00:11:49,842 --> 00:11:54,508
An old woman like me is useless, too.

104
00:11:54,508 --> 00:11:55,758
When I make soup,

105
00:11:55,758 --> 00:11:59,700
I can only find some wild vegetable leaves.

106
00:12:05,508 --> 00:12:07,242
Just take it for now.

107
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:09,867
We can always find more later.

108
00:12:11,008 --> 00:12:12,467
Thank you.

109
00:12:12,467 --> 00:12:13,717
Thank you, young man.

110
00:12:13,717 --> 00:12:15,508
You're all good people.

111
00:12:15,508 --> 00:12:17,867
Eat up, eat up.

112
00:12:18,633 --> 00:12:20,283
Hurry and eat.

113
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:44,950
What's the problem?

114
00:12:46,592 --> 00:12:48,050
The fuel line is clogged.

115
00:12:48,050 --> 00:12:49,675
Is it an easy fix?

116
00:12:49,675 --> 00:12:52,908
It's not hard, it just takes time.

117
00:12:54,842 --> 00:12:57,883
Come on, follow me to the eastern woods.

118
00:12:57,883 --> 00:13:00,550
I still have to clear the fuel line.

119
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:02,300
I plan to leave tomorrow.

120
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:04,200
We need to stock up on food.

121
00:13:06,050 --> 00:13:07,550
Tomorrow?

122
00:13:07,550 --> 00:13:09,992
Then we should fix the boat even sooner.

123
00:13:12,592 --> 00:13:13,592
How about this?

124
00:13:13,592 --> 00:13:15,675
You go hunting, and I'll keep fixing it.

125
00:13:15,675 --> 00:13:17,050
No.

126
00:13:17,050 --> 00:13:18,700
We go together.

127
00:13:20,083 --> 00:13:22,250
Why? You're enough for hunting on your own.

128
00:13:22,250 --> 00:13:24,250
And you can't help with the boat.

129
00:13:24,250 --> 00:13:26,500
You want to leave soon,
but you won't divide the work.

130
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:29,400
- What exactly do you want?
- I can't leave you alone.

131
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,066
It's dangerous.

132
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:43,958
Dangerous?

133
00:13:43,958 --> 00:13:45,208
Lie.

134
00:13:45,208 --> 00:13:46,250
I'm going with you,

135
00:13:46,250 --> 00:13:48,333
but that doesn't mean I'm your prisoner.

136
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:51,108
I'm fixing the boat to help you, after all.

137
00:14:02,666 --> 00:14:04,416
We don't have much time.

138
00:14:04,416 --> 00:14:06,900
Let's not waste it keeping tabs on each other.

139
00:14:36,291 --> 00:14:37,625
You're back.

140
00:14:37,625 --> 00:14:39,691
This chicken is so fat.

141
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:43,775
Look, a chicken.

142
00:14:57,875 --> 00:14:59,775
Are you going out again?

143
00:15:04,458 --> 00:15:06,275
What took you so long?

144
00:15:07,292 --> 00:15:09,525
What? Afraid I'll run away?

145
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:11,916
Madam.

146
00:15:11,916 --> 00:15:12,958
We're having chicken tonight.

147
00:15:12,958 --> 00:15:14,125
Your friend is really impressive.

148
00:15:14,125 --> 00:15:16,441
We haven't had meat in a long time.

149
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:28,150
Your hands are dirty. Go wash up first.

